  "instance_name": "camel_urine_medicine_claim",
  "label": "Claim that Camel Urine is Medicine",
  "description": "This is a real-world claim rooted in traditional Islamic medicine (Hikma) and some folk remedies, which references the hadith (sayings of the Prophet Muhammad) where he is reported to have used camel urine for medicinal purposes. The meme misrepresents this as a 'perfect' or 'divine' endorsement, ignoring the context and the fact that such practices are not universally accepted or endorsed by mainstream Islamic scholars or modern medicine. The meme uses this claim to create a false equivalence with the prohibition of pork, which is a core tenet of Islamic dietary law.",
